# Implementation Plan: MediSense Audit Logging & Abuse Detection System

Build the complete, privacy-guarded audit logging system and automated abuse detection pipeline in `com.medisense.audit`, featuring 35 distinct `AuditEvent` types, append-only PostgreSQL storage, SHA256 query text hashing, `@Async` non-blocking execution, Redis Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) retry processing, automated pattern-based abuse detection, and feedback into `RateLimitFilter`.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Audit Logging Architecture & Security Constraints**:
> - **35 `AuditEvent` Types**: Covers full lifecycle from auth (`AUTH_LOGIN_SUCCESS`, `AUTH_ACCOUNT_LOCKED`) to RAG (`QUERY_CLASSIFIED_PRESCRIPTIVE`, `CITATION_VERIFICATION_PASSED`) and translation (`TRANSLATION_INTEGRITY_FAILED`).
> - **Append-Only Database Rules**: Enforced via PostgreSQL rules `no_update_audit` and `no_delete_audit` on `audit_log` table.
> - **Privacy Enforcement**: Query texts stored ONLY as SHA256 hashes (`query_text_hash`). Drug names and lab values strictly stripped from `event_detail`.
> - **Non-Blocking Execution & Resilience**: `@Async` thread pool writes. Failed DB writes push to Redis list `audit:dlq` and log ERROR alerts. `DlqRetryJob` retries DLQ items every 5 minutes.
> - **Abuse Detection & Throttling**: `@Scheduled` `AbuseDetectionJob` flags abusive users (>10 prescriptive attempts/hr) for 24h and abusive IPs (>50 rate limit breaches/hr) for 1h in Redis. `RateLimitFilter` checks flags and cuts tier limits by 50%.

